<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<subsection xml:id="student_learning_outcomes" label="student_learning_outcomes" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Student Learning Outcomes</title>
  <p>
    Upon successful completion of this course, students will be able to
    <ul>
      <li>state the definitions and fundamental theorems concerning rings, modules, and groups,</li>
      <li>verify whether a given set with operations forms a ring, module, or group, and whether a given map is a homomorphism,</li>
      <li>compute in concrete examples, including modular arithmetic, polynomial rings, and cyclic groups,</li>
      <li>construct examples and counterexamples distinguishing algebraic structures and their properties,</li>
      <li>write clear, logically correct proofs of statements in elementary abstract algebra, and identify gaps or errors in a proposed proof.</li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</subsection>
